---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const emailPitch = "mailto:olga@okad.agency?subject=UGC%20brand%20outreach%20%E2%80%94%20tell%20us%20about%20your%20goals";
const emailGeneral = "mailto:olga@okad.agency?subject=UGC%20outreach%20%E2%80%94%20general%20inquiry";
const calHref = "https://calendly.com/okad_calls/first";
---

<Layout
  title="How to Pitch Brands as a UGC Creator — The Full Playbook | OKAD"
  description="A complete guide to pitching brands as a UGC creator: pre-pitch preparation, finding decision-makers, cold email templates, DM scripts, follow-up sequences, rate negotiation, and common mistakes to avoid."
>
  <Header />
  <main>

    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="pt-20 md:pt-24 pb-10 text-center bg-bg">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-[12px] font-medium text-accent bg-[rgba(99,102,241,.06)] border border-[rgba(99,102,241,.18)] rounded-full px-3.5 py-1.5 mb-6">
          Open reference &middot; September 2026
        </div>
        <h1 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(28px,5vw,48px)] leading-[1.1] tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink mb-4">
          How to Pitch Brands: <span class="text-accent">The Full Playbook</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-[18px] text-ink-2 max-w-[600px] mx-auto leading-[1.6] mb-8">
          Brand deals do not arrive because you exist on the internet. This guide covers the entire outreach arc &mdash; preparation, cold emails, DM scripts, follow-ups, rate negotiation, and the mistakes that sink most creators' pipelines.
        </p>
        <div class="flex gap-3 justify-center flex-wrap mb-8">
          <a href={emailPitch} class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-xl font-sans text-[14px] font-semibold bg-accent text-white hover:bg-accent-hover transition-all no-underline">Get outreach help &rarr;</a>
          <a href={calHref} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-xl font-sans text-[14px] font-semibold bg-card text-ink border border-border hover:border-accent hover:text-accent transition-all no-underline">Book a call &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-5 flex-wrap justify-center font-mono text-[12px] text-muted">
          <span>6 email templates</span>
          <span>DM scripts</span>
          <span>Follow-up cadence</span>
          <span>Rate negotiation</span>
          <span>15&ndash;20 pitches/wk</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- How it works grid -->
    <section class="py-8">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <h2 class="font-display text-[22px] font-bold tracking-[-0.02em] text-center mb-5">How Brand Outreach Works</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-3.5">
          <div class="bg-card border border-border rounded-[10px] p-4 text-center">
            <div class="text-[22px] mb-1.5">&#x1F3AF;</div>
            <h3 class="font-display text-[14px] font-semibold mb-1">Prepare &amp; Position</h3>
            <p class="text-[12px] text-muted leading-[1.4]">Build a clean portfolio, define your niche, gather proof points, and set up a professional email before you contact anyone.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-card border border-border rounded-[10px] p-4 text-center">
            <div class="text-[22px] mb-1.5">&#x1F4E7;</div>
            <h3 class="font-display text-[14px] font-semibold mb-1">Pitch &amp; Follow Up</h3>
            <p class="text-[12px] text-muted leading-[1.4]">Send targeted cold emails and DMs to decision-makers. Run a three-touch follow-up sequence that converts silence into conversations.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-card border border-border rounded-[10px] p-4 text-center">
            <div class="text-[22px] mb-1.5">&#x1F4B0;</div>
            <h3 class="font-display text-[14px] font-semibold mb-1">Negotiate &amp; Close</h3>
            <p class="text-[12px] text-muted leading-[1.4]">Name your price with confidence, present packages over unit prices, and handle objections professionally to close paid deals.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- TOC -->
    <section class="py-10 border-t border-b border-border">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-muted-2 mb-4">Contents</div>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-1.5">
          {[
            { num: "01", text: "Overview", href: "#overview" },
            { num: "02", text: "Pre-Pitch Preparation", href: "#preparation" },
            { num: "03", text: "Finding the Right Contact", href: "#contacts" },
            { num: "04", text: "Cold Email Templates", href: "#emails" },
            { num: "05", text: "DM Scripts", href: "#dms" },
            { num: "06", text: "Follow-Up Sequences", href: "#followup" },
            { num: "07", text: "Rate Negotiation", href: "#negotiation" },
            { num: "08", text: "Timing Your Outreach", href: "#timing" },
            { num: "09", text: "Subject Lines", href: "#subjects" },
            { num: "10", text: "Common Mistakes", href: "#mistakes" },
            { num: "11", text: "FAQ", href: "#faq" },
          ].map((item) => (
            <a href={item.href} class="flex items-center gap-2.5 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[14px] text-ink-2 font-medium hover:bg-bg-alt transition-colors no-underline">
              <span class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium text-accent min-w-[22px]">{item.num}</span>
              {item.text}
            </a>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 01 Overview -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="overview">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">01 &mdash; Overview</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Outreach is a system, not a one-off message</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Brand deals go to creators with sharp outreach skills, not the largest followings</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Treating outreach as a repeatable system is what separates booked creators from idle ones</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">This guide covers the entire arc from preparation through closing deals</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Brand deals do not arrive in your inbox because you exist on the internet. Creators with hundreds of thousands of followers sit idle, refreshing their DMs, while lesser-known creators with sharp outreach skills book three paid projects a month. The difference is never talent alone &mdash; it is whether you treat brand outreach as a repeatable system or leave it to chance.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">At OKAD, we manage creator networks and produce UGC campaigns for brands across e-commerce, SaaS, food and beverage, and lifestyle verticals. We have seen what lands in marketing managers' inboxes &mdash; and what gets deleted in under two seconds. This guide distills everything we have learned into a step-by-step process you can start running today, whether you have fifty followers or fifty thousand.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">What follows covers the entire arc: preparing before you send a single message, identifying the right person at each company, crafting emails and DMs that earn responses, building a follow-up cadence that converts silence into conversations, negotiating rates without leaving money behind, timing your outreach for maximum impact, and sidestepping the errors that sink most creators' pipelines.</p>
        <ul class="list-none p-0 space-y-2">
          <li class="flex items-baseline gap-2 py-1.5 text-ink-2"><strong class="text-ink min-w-[120px]">Target:</strong> 15&ndash;20 personalized pitches per week</li>
          <li class="flex items-baseline gap-2 py-1.5 text-ink-2"><strong class="text-ink min-w-[120px]">Channels:</strong> cold email (primary), DMs (bridge to email)</li>
          <li class="flex items-baseline gap-2 py-1.5 text-ink-2"><strong class="text-ink min-w-[120px]">Follow-ups:</strong> 3-touch sequence, spaced 3&ndash;7 days apart</li>
          <li class="flex items-baseline gap-2 py-1.5 text-ink-2"><strong class="text-ink min-w-[120px]">Templates:</strong> 6 email templates, 2 DM scripts, 3 follow-up messages</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 02 Pre-Pitch Preparation -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="preparation">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">02 &mdash; Preparation</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">What to do before you contact anyone</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Build a single, clean portfolio link with 4&ndash;6 of your strongest clips</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Define your content positioning in one sentence before you write any outreach</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">If your portfolio is not ready, stop and build it first</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Every brand contact you reach out to will do the same thing within ten seconds of opening your message: click whatever link you included and decide if you are credible. If that link leads to a disorganized Google Drive folder, a personal TikTok with no clear positioning, or worse, nothing at all &mdash; the conversation is over before it started.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">The preparation checklist</h3>
        <ol class="list-none p-0 counter-reset-step space-y-0">
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Build a single, clean portfolio link.</strong> Include four to six of your strongest UGC clips, a brief description of the niches and product categories you have created for (paid or unpaid work both count), a clear way to request your rates, and your contact information. A brand scanning your work does not want to scroll through forty random clips. They want to see four great ones that feel relevant to what they sell.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Define your content positioning.</strong> Can you articulate in one sentence what kind of content you make, who it resonates with, and what makes your approach distinct? The creators who stand out are the ones who can say: "I produce unscripted product demos for wellness brands, filmed in natural light with a conversational tone that performs well in paid social." That specificity signals professionalism.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Gather proof points.</strong> If previous content has driven measurable results &mdash; views, saves, click-through rates, conversion data &mdash; note those numbers. If you have worked with any recognizable brand, even on a small scale, make that visible. Social proof compresses the trust-building process from paragraphs to a single line.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Set up a professional email address.</strong> Sending outreach from a Gmail account with your birth year in the handle undercuts everything else. A custom domain is ideal; a clean, name-based address is the minimum.</li>
        </ol>

        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mt-6 mb-4">If your portfolio and positioning are not ready, stop here and build them first. Every template in this guide assumes you have a polished link to share.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 03 Finding Contacts -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="contacts">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">03 &mdash; Contacts</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">How to reach the person who can say yes</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Your pitch needs to reach someone with authority: marketing manager, partnerships lead, or founder</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Check social bios, LinkedIn, team pages, and tagged collaborations</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Reaching the right person is worth more than perfecting the wrong message</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Sending a pitch to a generic "info@" or "hello@" address is the outreach equivalent of tossing a message in a bottle into the ocean. Your email needs to reach someone with the authority and context to act on it &mdash; typically a marketing manager, a brand partnerships lead, or, at smaller companies, the founder themselves.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Where to find contacts</h3>
        <ol class="list-none p-0 counter-reset-step space-y-0">
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Start with social bios.</strong> Many DTC and e-commerce brands list a dedicated partnerships or press email directly in their Instagram or TikTok bio. This takes thirty seconds to check and is often the most direct route.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Search LinkedIn strategically.</strong> Look up the company name combined with titles like "marketing manager," "influencer partnerships," "content lead," or "brand manager." At smaller companies with under fifty employees, one person typically manages the entire creator program.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Check the company website.</strong> About pages, team pages, and career listings often reveal names and roles. Once you have a name, most companies follow a predictable email format: first@company.com, first.last@company.com, or firstinitial.last@company.com.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Look at tagged collaborations.</strong> If another creator has posted sponsored content for the brand, check whether they tagged a specific person or thanked someone by name in comments. That person likely manages creator relationships.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Use DMs only as a last resort.</strong> Direct messages on social platforms can work as an opening move, but they get buried in request folders and lack the formality needed for discussing budgets and contracts. When you do open via DM, move the conversation to email as quickly as possible.</li>
        </ol>

        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mt-6 mb-4">Finding the right contact is the most labor-intensive part of outreach. At OKAD, when we run creator campaigns, this research phase is where most of the upfront time goes &mdash; because reaching the right person is worth more than perfecting the message sent to the wrong one.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 04 Cold Email Templates -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="emails">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">04 &mdash; Email Templates</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Cold emails that earn responses</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Answer four questions in the first few lines: why this brand, what you create, what you propose, next step</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Keep every message under 150 words</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Six templates below cover every common scenario</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">A pitch that works answers four questions within the first few lines, without making the reader dig for the answers:</p>
        <ul class="pl-5 mb-4 space-y-2 text-ink-2">
          <li><strong class="text-ink">Why are you reaching out to this specific brand?</strong> Proof that the message is not copy-pasted.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ink">What do you create?</strong> Your niche, format, and platform in one sentence.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ink">What are you proposing?</strong> Paid content, affiliate arrangement, whitelisting rights &mdash; name the structure.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-ink">What is the next step?</strong> One simple action, not a multi-paragraph negotiation.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Every template below follows a five-part skeleton: a specific opener, a brief introduction of who you are, a statement of fit, a concrete offer, and a low-friction ask. Adapt the bracketed sections to each brand.</p>

        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-border bg-card mb-6">
          <table class="w-full border-collapse text-[14px]">
            <thead class="bg-bg">
              <tr>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Template</th>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Best for</th>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Subject line</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Standard Cold Pitch</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">No prior relationship</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Content concept for [Brand]</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Existing Customer</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">You genuinely use the product</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Already using [Product] &mdash; content partnership idea</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Paid Media Pitch</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Brand running creator-style ads</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Ad creative for [Brand] &mdash; UGC creator</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Revenue-Share</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Brands without upfront budgets</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Performance partnership &mdash; [Your Name] x [Brand]</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Past-Client Re-engagement</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Former clients (warmest pipeline)</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Round two? New content concepts for [Brand]</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink">Open-Call Application</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink-2">Brand publicly seeking creators</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink-2">Applying &mdash; [Your Name], UGC creator for [Brand]</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Template 1: The Standard Cold Pitch</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Use this as your default when reaching out to a brand you have no prior relationship with.</p>
        <blockquote class="border-l-[3px] border-accent pl-5 py-3 my-6 bg-accent-bg rounded-r-lg">
          <p class="text-ink-2 mb-0 text-[15px] leading-[1.7]">
            <strong class="text-ink">Subject:</strong> Content concept for [Brand]<br><br>
            Hi [Name],<br><br>
            I came across [Brand] through [specific detail: a recent product drop, an ad I saw running on Meta, something genuine]. The way you position [product/category] stood out to me.<br><br>
            I produce short-form UGC in [your niche] &mdash; [one-line description of your style, e.g., "fast-paced product walkthroughs with a casual, unscripted feel"]. I think there is a natural overlap between what I create and what your audience responds to.<br><br>
            I would love to put together a paid content package for [Brand] &mdash; a few short videos designed for your paid ads or organic feed. My portfolio is here: [link].<br><br>
            Happy to share rates and turnaround details if this is of interest.<br><br>
            Best,<br>
            [Your Name]<br>
            [Portfolio link] | [Social handle]
          </p>
        </blockquote>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4"><strong class="text-ink">Why this structure works:</strong> the opener proves relevance, the deliverable is named explicitly, and the call to action requires only a yes or no. There is nothing to decode.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Template 2: The Existing Customer Angle</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">This is the highest-converting pitch format &mdash; use it whenever you genuinely use the product.</p>
        <blockquote class="border-l-[3px] border-accent pl-5 py-3 my-6 bg-accent-bg rounded-r-lg">
          <p class="text-ink-2 mb-0 text-[15px] leading-[1.7]">
            <strong class="text-ink">Subject:</strong> Already using [Product] &mdash; content partnership idea<br><br>
            Hi [Name],<br><br>
            I have been a genuine [Product] customer for [timeframe], and I consistently find myself creating content around it organically. It felt like the right time to reach out and see if there is an opportunity to formalize that into a paid collaboration.<br><br>
            I create [niche] UGC &mdash; portfolio here: [link]. I would love to develop a small content package for [Brand] built around the same authentic angle I already take with your product, just with a proper brief and structure behind it.<br><br>
            Can I send over a few content concepts and my rates?<br><br>
            Thanks,<br>
            [Your Name]
          </p>
        </blockquote>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Template 3: The Paid Media Pitch</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Use this when you want to position your content specifically for the brand's advertising campaigns.</p>
        <blockquote class="border-l-[3px] border-accent pl-5 py-3 my-6 bg-accent-bg rounded-r-lg">
          <p class="text-ink-2 mb-0 text-[15px] leading-[1.7]">
            <strong class="text-ink">Subject:</strong> Ad creative for [Brand] &mdash; UGC creator<br><br>
            Hi [Name],<br><br>
            I noticed [Brand] is running creator-style ads across Meta and TikTok &mdash; that is exactly the format I specialize in. Portfolio here: [link].<br><br>
            I would like to propose a small batch of UGC videos engineered specifically for paid performance &mdash; hook-driven openings, product demos, or testimonial-style content, depending on what fits your current campaign goals.<br><br>
            Usage rights for paid social can be included in the package. Let me know if you would like a rate breakdown.<br><br>
            Best,<br>
            [Your Name]
          </p>
        </blockquote>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Template 4: The Revenue-Share Proposal</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Effective for brands that may not have large upfront budgets but offer ongoing earning potential.</p>
        <blockquote class="border-l-[3px] border-accent pl-5 py-3 my-6 bg-accent-bg rounded-r-lg">
          <p class="text-ink-2 mb-0 text-[15px] leading-[1.7]">
            <strong class="text-ink">Subject:</strong> Performance partnership &mdash; [Your Name] x [Brand]<br><br>
            Hi [Name],<br><br>
            I produce UGC in [niche] and believe there is genuine audience overlap between my content and [Brand]'s customer base. Instead of a flat-fee project, I would like to explore a commission-based or affiliate arrangement &mdash; I create content, drive tracked sales through a code or link, and we both benefit from the performance.<br><br>
            Portfolio: [link]<br><br>
            If you already run an affiliate program, I would love to be considered. If not, I am happy to discuss what that structure could look like.<br><br>
            Thanks,<br>
            [Your Name]
          </p>
        </blockquote>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Template 5: The Past-Client Re-engagement</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Former clients represent your warmest pipeline. Do not let them forget you.</p>
        <blockquote class="border-l-[3px] border-accent pl-5 py-3 my-6 bg-accent-bg rounded-r-lg">
          <p class="text-ink-2 mb-0 text-[15px] leading-[1.7]">
            <strong class="text-ink">Subject:</strong> Round two? New content concepts for [Brand]<br><br>
            Hi [Name],<br><br>
            Working together on [previous project] was genuinely one of my highlights this quarter. Since then, I have been experimenting with [new format/trend/angle], and I think it could translate really well for [Brand].<br><br>
            Would you be open to another collaboration? I can send a few concept ideas whenever works.<br><br>
            Best,<br>
            [Your Name]
          </p>
        </blockquote>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Template 6: The Open-Call Application</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">When a brand publicly announces they are seeking creators, use a focused, efficient response.</p>
        <blockquote class="border-l-[3px] border-accent pl-5 py-3 my-6 bg-accent-bg rounded-r-lg">
          <p class="text-ink-2 mb-0 text-[15px] leading-[1.7]">
            <strong class="text-ink">Subject:</strong> Applying &mdash; [Your Name], UGC creator for [Brand/Campaign]<br><br>
            Hi [Name],<br><br>
            Saw you are looking for UGC creators for [campaign/program]. I create [niche] content and believe my approach is a strong match &mdash; portfolio and samples here: [link].<br><br>
            Happy to share rates or jump on a brief call if helpful. Would love to be part of this.<br><br>
            Best,<br>
            [Your Name]
          </p>
        </blockquote>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 05 DM Scripts -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="dms">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">05 &mdash; DM Scripts</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">When social messages are your only door</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">DMs are a bridge to email, not the negotiation venue</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Never negotiate scope, rates, or deliverables inside a DM thread</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Open the door, establish interest, transition to email</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Direct messages should be treated as a bridge to email, not as the negotiation venue. DM threads get buried, lack threading, and feel informal in ways that make discussing budgets and contracts awkward. That said, some brands &mdash; particularly founder-led or very small companies &mdash; operate DM-first, and reaching them any other way is impractical.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Short DM for Instagram or TikTok</h3>
        <blockquote class="border-l-[3px] border-accent pl-5 py-3 my-6 bg-accent-bg rounded-r-lg">
          <p class="text-ink-2 mb-0 text-[15px] leading-[1.7]">
            Hey [Name] &mdash; I create [niche] UGC content and think there could be a solid fit for paid content for [Brand]. Here is my portfolio: [link]. Happy to share more details here or over email if you have one. Let me know!
          </p>
        </blockquote>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">DM after engaging with their content</h3>
        <blockquote class="border-l-[3px] border-accent pl-5 py-3 my-6 bg-accent-bg rounded-r-lg">
          <p class="text-ink-2 mb-0 text-[15px] leading-[1.7]">
            Hey! Been following your content for a while &mdash; your [specific post/campaign] really caught my attention. I produce similar style UGC and would love to create something for [Brand]. Portfolio: [link]. Is email the best way to discuss?
          </p>
        </blockquote>

        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4"><strong class="text-ink">The rule:</strong> never negotiate scope, rates, or deliverables inside a DM thread. Use the message to open the door, establish interest, and transition to email where the real conversation can happen properly.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Mid CTA -->
    <section class="py-10">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="bg-dark rounded-2xl p-10 md:p-14 text-center">
