        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Frequently asked questions</h2>

        {[
          { q: "Can I pitch brands if I have almost no followers?", a: "Absolutely. Most UGC deals are content purchases — brands are buying videos they can run as ads or post on their own channels, not paying for your personal reach. Your portfolio and the quality of your work matter far more than your follower count. Target brands that are specifically seeking UGC creators rather than influencer-style partnerships." },
          { q: "What are the essential components of a UGC pitch email?", a: "Five elements: a personalized opener that demonstrates you researched the brand, a single line about who you are and what you create, a clear statement of fit between your content and their product, a specific proposal (paid UGC, affiliate, ad creative), and one frictionless next step. The entire message should stay under 150 words." },
          { q: "How many pitches should I send each week?", a: "If you are serious about building a consistent deal flow, aim for fifteen to twenty targeted pitches per week. Cold outreach naturally has low response rates, so volume paired with genuine personalization — not spam — is what produces a reliable stream of opportunities." },
          { q: "What is the best way to find a brand contact's email?", a: "Check their social media bios for a partnerships email first. Then search LinkedIn for marketing or partnership roles at the company. Then look at the brand's website for team member names and deduce their email format. Direct messages are a last option, not a first choice." },
          { q: "Should I include pricing in my initial outreach?", a: "No. Offer to send rates once the brand expresses interest rather than leading with numbers. This keeps your first message focused on demonstrating fit, and it gives you room to tailor pricing after you understand what the brand actually needs." },
          { q: "How long should I wait between follow-ups?", a: "Three to four days after your initial pitch for the first follow-up, approximately one week after that for the second, and then a final closing message if you still have not heard back. Three total touchpoints is a professional and effective rhythm." },
          { q: "Is email or DM more effective for brand outreach?", a: "Email is almost always more effective for substantive outreach. It signals professionalism, supports proper threading, and is where budgets and contracts get discussed. Use DMs only when you cannot find an email, when the brand is clearly DM-first, or as a light initial touch before transitioning to email." },
          { q: "How do I handle a brand that offers only product, no payment?", a: "It is perfectly acceptable to decline or to counter-propose a hybrid arrangement: product plus a flat fee for the content. Be polite but clear about your professional rates. Some creators accept product-only deals early in their career to build portfolio examples, but this should be a strategic choice rather than a default." },
        ].map((item) => (
